  "title": "Chat conversations hardcode limit=100 with no pagination, silently drops older conversations",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: business-logic. Severity: P1. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The chat page fetches conversations with `?limit=100` (line 69) and messages with `?limit=100` (line 83), but never provides pagination or infinite scroll. Suppliers with more than 100 conversations will never see older ones. Similarly, conversations with more than 100 messages will show only the 100 most recent with no way to scroll back further. The BNPL page has the same problem (DA6-SUP-002) but chat is more critical since message history has legal/business significance.",
